# ─── foundry ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
contracts/out/
contracts/cache/
contracts/lib/forge-std/.git

# contracts/broadcast is deliberately NOT ignored here. `forge init` writes a
# nested contracts/.gitignore containing `!/broadcast`, and a nested ignore file
# wins over a parent rule for paths inside it — so a `contracts/broadcast/` line
# here would silently do nothing and read as protection that isn't there.
# Foundry's convention is the right one anyway: real deployment logs are a public
# audit trail (they carry tx hashes, addresses and constructor args, never keys),
# while local anvil (31337) and dry-runs are excluded by the nested file.

# ─── the graph ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
subgraph/generated/
subgraph/build/

# ─── rust / substreams ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
target/
*.spkg

# ─── env and secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
# MCP server configs carry Authorization headers in plaintext.
.mcp.json

# ─── logs and os ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.DS_Store
coverage/
.vscode/
.idea/

# dev server output — separate from .next so `next dev` and `next build` can coexist
.next-dev/

# rust build output
substreams/**/target/
*.spkg

# Alternate Next.js build outputs (NEXT_DIST_DIR) used to build without disturbing a
# running server — same artefacts as .next, same reason to never commit them.
.next-*

# Vercel CLI link state — contains the project/org id, not a secret, but it is
# machine-local and the project is already Git-linked in the dashboard.
.vercel
.env*
# Re-assert the exception. This `.env*` is broader than the `.env` / `.env.*` pair above and, being
# later in the file, it overrode their `!.env.example` negation — silently ignoring every
# .env.example that was not already tracked. Files already in the index kept working, which is what
# made it invisible: only NEW example files disappeared.
!.env.example
